.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:1:# ADR-0123: Typed Claim Feedback Semantics
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:6:**Extends:** [ADR-0113](0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md), [ADR-0114](0114-scoring-unification.md), [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) (SubjectAttribution amendment)
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:7:**Closes:** "v1.4.0 Claim Feedback and Prompt Granularity Review" — 7 open decisions
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:11:[ADR-0114](0114-scoring-unification.md) R1.7 placed `user_feedback_weight` as a canonical scoring factor and referenced a `FeedbackAction` enum with placeholder values `StillTrue | Outdated | WrongSource`. [ADR-0113](0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md) §6 declared the agent trust-ledger updates as "User accepts an agent claim → α += 1 / User contradicts → β += 1" without typing accept vs. contradict.
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:20:Without typed semantics, feedback collected in v1.4.0 would not be translatable into the trust-compiler updates ADR-0114 specifies. **Trust Compiler ships in v1.4.0 spine; therefore feedback semantics close in v1.4.0 spine.** The 7 open decisions from the Linear review are answered below in §3.
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:53:    /// → consumes the typed `SubjectRef` from ADR-0105 SubjectAttribution amendment.
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:79:    ///   no source penalty; feeds ADR-0108 surface privacy policy.
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:97:    pub subject: SubjectRef,                  // From ADR-0105 SubjectAttribution amendment
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:108:### 3. The 7 open decisions, closed
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:122:The Trust Compiler (DOS-5) consumes `ClaimFeedback` via the `user_feedback_weight` factor (per ADR-0114 R1.3, the factor takes pre-computed `age_days`, not a clock). Per-action deltas:
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:140:- `scoring::factors::user_feedback_weight(feedback: Option<&UserFeedbackInput>)` (ADR-0114 R1.3) consumes a `UserFeedbackInput { action: FeedbackAction, age_days: f64 }`. Pure; the extractor pulls latest feedback per claim per ADR-0114 §2.
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:141:- ADR-0113 §6 agent-ledger updates are typed by `FeedbackAction` rather than abstract "accept/contradict" — see §4.
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:142:- ADR-0113 §5 tombstone behavior is now triggered by `WrongSubject` (per-subject tombstone) and `MarkFalse` (broad tombstone), not by an untyped UI gesture.
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:146:### 6. Subject correction interplay (ADR-0105 amendment)
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:148:`WrongSubject { corrected_to }` is the user-side complement to ADR-0105's `SubjectAttribution` substrate primitive. Behavior:
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:162:4. Found corroboration → claim corroboration record (ADR-0113 R1.6); user notified.
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:181:- `WrongSubject` becomes a substrate-level operation pairing cleanly with ADR-0105 `SubjectAttribution`. Subject mistakes do not punish sources.
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:183:- The 7 open decisions are answered before kickoff. No spec churn during the spine push.
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:194:- No new tables beyond `claim_feedback` and `claim_repair_job` (skeleton). ADR-0113's existing tables absorb the structural updates.
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:199:- [ADR-0105: Provenance as First-Class Output](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) — `SubjectAttribution` amendment supplies `SubjectRef` consumed by `WrongSubject`.
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:200:- [ADR-0113: Human and Agent Analysis as First-Class Claim Sources](0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md) — agent-ledger updates typed via this ADR (§6 amended by §4 here).
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:201:- [ADR-0114: Scoring Unification](0114-scoring-unification.md) — `user_feedback_weight` factor consumes the typed action; R1.3 `UserFeedbackInput` shape adopted here.
.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:202:- v1.4.0 Claim Feedback and Prompt Granularity Review (Linear doc 0b668ff1c80a) — sourcing of the 7 decisions closed in §3.
