.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:1:# ADR-0125: Claim Anatomy v2 — Temporal Scope, Sensitivity, Claim Type Registry
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:6:**Extends:** [ADR-0113](0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md), [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md), [ADR-0114](0114-scoring-unification.md)
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:7:**Pattern parallel:** [ADR-0115](0115-signal-granularity-audit.md) Signal Policy Registry
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:15:3. **Claim type taxonomy** (Review §15) — currently free-form strings; should be a closed-but-extensible registry following the ADR-0115 Signal Policy Registry pattern.
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:17:This ADR is the substrate allowance: schema fields + types + registry mechanism. Downstream enforcement (freshness scoring, render gates) is named per-dimension and lands in v1.4.1+.
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:51:ALTER TABLE intelligence_claims ADD COLUMN temporal_scope TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'state';
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:82:ALTER TABLE intelligence_claims ADD COLUMN sensitivity TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'internal';
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:93:This ADR introduces `ClaimTypeRegistry` — a compile-time exhaustive const slice mapping every legal `claim_type` to its metadata:
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:97:    /// Canonical string written into the `intelligence_claims.claim_type` column.
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:110:    /// Commit policy class per ADR-0113 §3 — most types are Standard;
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:149:- New claim types require an ADR amendment (or registry-extension PR with documented rationale linking back to this ADR).
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:150:- The pattern parallels [ADR-0115](0115-signal-granularity-audit.md) Signal Policy Registry — same exhaustiveness check shape.
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:185:- Registry maintenance burden — every new claim type requires a registration PR. Mitigated by mirroring ADR-0115 Signal Policy Registry pattern (proven on signals; same author cadence).
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:191:- The registry pattern matches an existing precedent (ADR-0115); no new architectural concept.
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:195:- [ADR-0113: Human and Agent Analysis as First-Class Claim Sources](0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md) — claim row schema; this ADR adds three fields.
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:196:- [ADR-0105: Provenance as First-Class Output](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) — `Provenance.warnings` interacts with sensitivity at render-time masking.
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:197:- [ADR-0114: Scoring Unification](0114-scoring-unification.md) — `freshness_weight` factor will consult `temporal_scope` in v1.4.1.
.docs/decisions/0125-claim-anatomy-temporal-sensitivity-typeregistry.md:198:- [ADR-0115: Signal Granularity, Policy Registry, and Durable Invalidation](0115-signal-granularity-audit.md) — pattern parallel for the claim type registry's compile-time exhaustiveness.
