.docs/decisions/0030-weekly-prep-with-daily-refresh.md:79:ADR-0006's determinism boundary still applies **per-operation** where AI enrichment is needed. `meeting:prep` and `/today`'s overview synthesis are the two operations that involve Phase 2 (Claude). The others are purely deterministic.
.docs/decisions/0030-weekly-prep-with-daily-refresh.md:87:- Feature toggles (ADR-0039) can enable/disable individual operations (e.g., email triage off, meeting prep on)
.docs/decisions/0030-weekly-prep-with-daily-refresh.md:94:This ADR's decomposition was never fully implemented. The per-meeting prep operation exists inside `prepare_today()` but is not independently callable. `prepare_week()` generates only `week-overview.json` (summary) — no individual meeting preps. Calendar polling detects changes but doesn't trigger `meeting:prep`.
