.docs/decisions/0066-meeting-intelligence-package.md:219:## 2026-02-18 Alignment Note (ADR-0081)
.docs/decisions/0066-meeting-intelligence-package.md:221:ADR-0081 (Event-Driven Meeting Intelligence, 0.13.0) builds on this ADR and extends the `MeetingIntelligence` concept:
.docs/decisions/0066-meeting-intelligence-package.md:224:- **Lifecycle starts at detection, not day-of.** This ADR's persistence lifecycle shows "Daily briefing runs → Prep enriched." ADR-0081 shifts this: intelligence enriches when the meeting is first detected on the calendar (via weekly run or calendar polling), not on the day of the meeting. The `MeetingIntelligence` record exists days to weeks before the meeting.
.docs/decisions/0066-meeting-intelligence-package.md:226:- **Implementation:** I326 implements the lifecycle. Phase 1 of this ADR (route migration to `meetingId`, `get_meeting_intelligence` command) is a prerequisite and should ship first or concurrently with I326.
.docs/decisions/0004-hybrid-json-markdown-architecture.md:1:# ADR-0004: Hybrid JSON + Markdown architecture
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:1:# ADR-0081: Event-Driven Meeting Intelligence
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:7:**Builds on:** [ADR-0030](0030-weekly-prep-with-daily-refresh.md) (composable workflow operations), [ADR-0066](0066-meeting-intelligence-package.md) (meeting intelligence package), [ADR-0080](0080-signal-intelligence-architecture.md) (signal intelligence architecture)
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:8:**Enriches:** [ADR-0052](0052-week-page-redesign.md) (week page redesign — readiness checks evolve into intelligence quality indicators)
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:26:**3. Internal meetings get second-class intelligence.** The classification in `classify.rs` routes meetings into three tiers: `account-prep` (full entity intelligence), `person-prep` (thinner context), and `no-prep` (personal, all-hands, training). Internal 1:1s and team syncs get person-prep at best. But with internal teams becoming accounts (ADR-0070), there's no reason an Engineering team standup shouldn't get entity-quality intelligence from the team entity.
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:30:### What Changed Since ADR-0030
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:32:ADR-0030 (Composable Workflow Operations) proposed exactly the right decomposition: `meeting:prep` as an independent atomic operation callable by any orchestrator, with the weekly orchestrator generating preps for the full week and calendar polling triggering preps for newly detected meetings. That was written February 2026 during the Rust migration.
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:36:ADR-0066 (Meeting Intelligence Package) proposed the right data model: a unified `MeetingIntelligence` struct that accumulates over a meeting's lifecycle (pre-meeting → during → post-meeting → permanent), with ID-based routing and a single `get_meeting_intelligence` command.
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:38:ADR-0080 (Signal Intelligence Architecture) proposed the right event infrastructure: a signal bus where data sources produce typed, weighted, time-decaying signals that drive entity resolution, enrichment, and proactive hygiene.
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:40:The architecture is designed. This ADR implements the operational model that brings it to life.
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:56:Every meeting on the user's calendar (except all-hands: 50+ attendees) has a **meeting intelligence record** that is born when the meeting is detected and lives permanently. This is the `MeetingIntelligence` struct from ADR-0066, but with a crucial change: it's created *immediately on detection*, not on the day of the meeting.
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:63:| **Initial enrichment** | Async, within minutes of detection | `meeting:prep` (ADR-0030) generates intelligence: attendee context, entity intelligence, historical notes, agenda (calendar description or AI-generated), talking points, signals. Written to SQLite. |
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:66:| **Post-meeting capture** | Transcript attached | Outcomes, decisions, actions, wins, risks captured. Intelligence record augmented, not replaced. |
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:69:The intelligence record grows — nothing is discarded. Pre-meeting intelligence doesn't disappear when outcomes arrive (ADR-0066's core decision). The record is always accessible via `get_meeting_intelligence(meeting_id)`.
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:92:The key change: `training` and `personal` no longer skip entirely — they get minimal records that serve as learning nodes for future encounters. `team_sync` meetings associated with internal team entities (ADR-0070) get full entity intelligence, not thin person-prep.
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:98:**Weekly orchestrator (revised from ADR-0030):**
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:182:- Readiness checks (ADR-0052) evolve from "no agenda" / "no prep" to intelligence-quality-driven: "3 meetings with sparse context" / "2 meetings with stale intelligence"
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:233:1. Records the signal in `signal_events` (ADR-0080)
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:269:**Target ratio:** For a typical week of 50 meetings, the weekly run should produce ~10-15 AI calls (entity-clustered), not 50. Daily runs should produce 1 AI call (overview narrative) plus 0-3 signal refreshes for today's meetings. The system should be able to function (at Developing quality) with zero AI calls if Claude Code is unavailable — graceful degradation per ADR-0042.
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:279:- **Internal meetings stop being second-class.** Team syncs, 1:1s, cross-functional reviews all get intelligence appropriate to their context. Internal team entities (ADR-0070) provide the same enrichment depth as external accounts.
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:330:- ADR-0030: Composable workflow operations (the `meeting:prep` atomic operation)
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:331:- ADR-0052: Week page redesign (readiness checks, day shapes)
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:332:- ADR-0066: Meeting intelligence package (`MeetingIntelligence` struct, unified lifecycle)
.docs/decisions/0081-event-driven-meeting-intelligence.md:333:- ADR-0070: Internal team entities (internal meetings get entity-quality intelligence)
