     1	//! Unified async/sync database connection pool (DOS-* DbService refactor).
     2	//!
     3	//! Single source of truth for all DB access in the process. Replaces the old
     4	//! dual model (tokio_rusqlite async pool + `ActionDb::open()` fresh-opens)
     5	//! that caused WAL races under SQLCipher: two connections reading the same
     6	//! mid-commit WAL frame would trigger HMAC verification failures ("file is
     7	//! not a database") because each fresh `rusqlite::Connection::open()` gets
     8	//! its own OS-level handle with no awareness of the pool writer's in-progress
     9	//! commit stream.
    10	//!
    11	//! Architecture (ADR followup, not yet numbered):
    12	//! - 1 writer connection and N readers, each owning a dedicated OS thread.
    13	//! - `.call(|conn| ...).await` and `.call_sync(|conn| ...)` submit closures to
    14	//!   the dedicated thread and await completion over channels.
    15	//! - A process-wide `GLOBAL` singleton lets `ActionDb::open()` route through
    16	//!   the pool instead of opening a fresh handle. If the pool is not yet
    17	//!   initialized (startup, tests) `ActionDb::open()` falls back to the
    18	//!   legacy fresh-open path.
    19	//! - Fresh opens can also be serialized through `open_fresh_serialized` to avoid
    20	//!   SQLCipher WAL read-verify races on `Connection::open()` verification.
    21	
    22	use std::any::Any;
    23	use std::path::PathBuf;
    24	use std::panic::{self, AssertUnwindSafe};
    25	use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicUsize, Ordering};
    26	use std::sync::{mpsc, Arc, Mutex as StdMutex};
    27	use std::thread;
